# =============================================================================
# Auris — Git ignore rules
#
# The two things that must never be tracked, and why they are called out here
# rather than left in a generic block:
#
#   local.properties  Holds the Supabase project URL and anon key. The anon key
#                     is designed to be public, but committing it to a public
#                     repository still enables someone to enumerate your project's
#                     data through the anon key's row-level-security scope and,
#                     more practically, means rotating the key requires a history
#                     rewrite. It also holds your machine-local SDK path, which is
#                     worthless to anyone else.
#
#   .toolchain/       A self-contained JDK, Gradle distribution, GRADLE_USER_HOME
#                     (the multi-GB dependency cache) and an Android AVD, all
#                     installed locally to keep builds reproducible without
#                     touching system packages. None of it belongs in git.
#
# Room's exported schemas under app/schemas/ are deliberately NOT ignored —
# MigrationTestHelper reads them from the test APK's assets, and a migration
# cannot be validated without the historical schema it migrated from.
# =============================================================================

# ---- Secrets and machine-local configuration --------------------------------
local.properties
**/local.properties

# ---- Toolchain installed locally for reproducible builds ---------------------
.toolchain/
.gradle-user-home/

# ---- Gradle ------------------------------------------------------------------
# `**/build/` rather than `/build`: the leading slash matches only the repository
# root, which would leave every Gradle *module's* build directory tracked —
# source-api/build, mock-extension/build and the rest.
.gradle/
**/.gradle/
**/build/
/build/

# Gradle wrapper: the JAR is generated by `gradle wrapper`, so it is ignored here
# and should be committed deliberately if this repo is ever built without a local
# Gradle. Uncomment if you want a fully self-contained checkout.
# gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties
!gradle/libs.versions.toml

# ---- Kotlin ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.kotlin_module/
.kotlin/
**/.kotlin/
kotlin-js-store/

# ---- Android -----------------------------------------------------------------
*.apk
# Exception: the signature tests need a real, genuinely-signed third-party APK, and building
# one locally would defeat the point (it would be signed by our own key).
!app/src/androidTest/fixtures/*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
*.class

# Release signing material. Keystore files and their properties must never be
# committed; a leaked upload key lets anyone publish an update attributed to you.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
signing.properties

# Build outputs and intermediates
/captures/
.cxx/
.externalNativeBuild/
**/.externalNativeBuild/
release/
output.json
output-metadata.json
proguard-*.txt

# Native libraries
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll

# ---- Android Studio / IntelliJ ------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
out/

# ---- IDE and editor ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.settings/
.classpath
.project
*.launch
.factorypath

# ---- Test and coverage ---------------------------------------------------------
/coverage/
reports/
htmlcov/
*.lcov
test-results/

# ---- Logs --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.hprof
hs_err_pid*

# ---- OS cruft -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini